pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% The same fabrication reached through CHECKED DELETION rather than `pbc`: with
% `strengthening_to_core on` a `delc` subproof is a proof by contradiction and registers no
% proofgoals either, so `proofgoal 1` fabricated one and closing it discharged the deletion
% obligation. The consequence is a different wrong verdict: a CORE constraint is deleted for
% free, and the formula `x1 AND ~x1` -- unsatisfiable -- was reported
% `s VERIFIED SATISFIABLE`.
f 2 ;
strengthening_to_core on;
delc 2 : : subproof
    proofgoal 1
        rup >= 1 ;
    qed;
qed;
sol x1 ;
output NONE;
conclusion SAT ;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
